{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface","excerpts":[["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:bandbreakpoint","","<p><strong>Theorem 1.4</strong> (constant values of the floor in the\nweights). <em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, and suppose every supported index\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>i</mi></math></span> satisfies <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span>. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>!</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. In particular,\ncancellation on the interval <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></math></span> forces <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>; and\nif every supported index is at least <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span> while <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, then some supported index is\nat least <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:carry-equivalence","an exact criterion from successive\npartial sums","<p><em> For <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>,\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>14</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi>m</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em>Moreover </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnalign=\"right left\" columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"bottom top\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>15</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> </mtext><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mtext>for all sufficiently large </mtext></mstyle><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>16</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>B</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>:</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>m</mi><mo>∤</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></math></span> with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>∤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>!</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:channel-radius","","<p><strong>Theorem 3.5</strong> (a lower bound for the support\nparameter). <em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>\nsatisfy </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>M</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Consequently no family\nsatisfying these hypotheses for all sufficiently large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi></math></span> has <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> eventually, and none\nhas <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:companion-orbit","rationality and factorial residues","<p><em> </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>!</mo><mi>C</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo><mo>≡</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mtext>for all sufficiently large </mtext></mstyle><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:gap-gcd","factorial-gap gcd","<p><em> For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></math></span>, the integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> divides <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:global-residue","a sufficient tail inequality","<p><em>\nSuppose that for every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi></math></span> there is a\nnatural parameter <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>25</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>blk</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is\nirrational.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:lcm-growth","common-denominator growth","<p><em> </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mtext> </mtext><mo>≥</mo><mtext> </mtext><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:lower-escape","lower-interval criterion","<p><em>\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>20</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>B</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>:</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>\nthe finite condition </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>21</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mi>m</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mtext>or</mtext></mstyle><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> implies the escape inequality in <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface.html#long68:eq:lower-escape\">(20)</a>. Cofinally\nmany instances of <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface.html#long68:eq:finite-escape\">(21)</a> therefore\nimply <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:moment-ideal","","<p><strong>Theorem 1.2</strong> (the set of attainable values of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi></math></span>). <em> Fix <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and a prime <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></math></span>. Put </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mfrac><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For finite integer vectors\nsupported on <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and cancelling\nall weighted sums <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></math></span>, the\npossible values of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi></math></span> are exactly\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>. The integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></math></span> is positive, is independent of the\neligible prime <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi></math></span>, and is attained\nby a vector of coefficients with gcd one, that is, by a primitive\nvector.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:normalform","divisibility of the difference","<p><em> For\nevery finite integer support and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> there is an integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:prime-pole","maximal prime-power survival","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi></math></span> be a prime dividing <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></math></span>, and put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> and\nwrite <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>e</mi></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></math></span>. Then, with inverses in <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>8</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mi>den</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mtext>in </mtext></mstyle><msub><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:product-lcm","product, least common multiple, pairwise\ngcd","<p><em> For positive integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munderover><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\" fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><munder><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:radius-constant","","<p><strong>Corollary 3.6</strong> (the asymptotic lower bound). <em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> for all sufficiently\nlarge <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi></math></span>. Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mtext> </mtext><mo>≥</mo><mtext> </mtext><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:residual-transparency","","<p><strong>Theorem 1.3</strong> (how the coefficient choices change the\nremainder). <em> For the vector in <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface.html#long68:eq:low-channel-basis\">(2)</a>,\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>ℛ</mi></mrow><mspace width=\"-0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The remainder series converges\nfor every finite vector supported away from index zero. A vector with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> has integral remainder, and any\ntwo finite vectors with the same value of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi></math></span> have remainders differing by an\ninteger.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:segment","segment inequality","<p><em> For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>10</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>≤</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">(</mo></mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:shift-family","a criterion for the shifts <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>","<p><em> For every integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, the series <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></math></span> is rational exactly when </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">⌈</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>m</mi><mo>!</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> for all sufficiently large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span>, and irrational exactly when that\nresidue is missed cofinally. The member <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span>, and the member <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, for which the scaled correction is\nalways <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn></math></span> and hence misses the\nresidue class at every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>,\nproving the irrationality of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:translator","","<p><strong>Theorem 1.5</strong> (changing just one weighted sum). <em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span> be prime and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, with every other coefficient\nzero. Then <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos68-factorial-reasoning-surface#long68:res:wilson-cofinality","cofinal first prime occurrences","<p><em> For every integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> there\nare a prime <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi></math></span> and an integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></math></span>, <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>\nfor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"]]}
